export default "## My teammate can't see my posts / tasks\nPosts, chats, tasks and CRM records are only shared inside one workspace. If a teammate can't see them, you're probably in different workspaces.\n\n1. Check the name at the top-left of the sidebar on both screens; it must be the same shared workspace (👥).\n2. The owner of that workspace opens Share and adds the teammate's email.\n3. The teammate opens the workspace menu (click the workspace name) and picks it.\nUseful actions: check, invite, switch\n\n## Invite a teammate\nOpen Share (top right) in a shared workspace, type their email and press Enter. Lumen emails them a one-click sign-in link (and you can also copy the link). Only the workspace owner can invite.\nUseful actions: invite\n\n## The invite email didn't arrive\n• Ask them to check Spam / Promotions; it comes from noreply@lumen-notes-cde2c.firebaseapp.com titled “Sign in to Lumen Notes”.\n• The free plan sends at most 5 invite emails per day. After that, use Share → Copy invite link and send it on WhatsApp or chat.\n• They must sign in with the exact email you invited.\n• Use the ✉️ button next to their name in Share to resend.\nUseful actions: invite\n\n## Workspaces and signing in\nLumen always needs you to sign in (Google or an emailed sign-in link). Every workspace is online and synced: the people you invite see the same tasks, chat, CRM and files live, on any device. Switch between workspaces from the workspace menu (click its name, top left).\nUseful actions: switch\n\n## Create a shared workspace\nSign in, then open the workspace menu (click the workspace name) → Create a new workspace…. A short setup asks how you'll use it and sets it up for you. Then invite people from the workspace menu or Settings → Manage access.\nUseful actions: newws\n\n## Remove someone from a workspace\nOwner only: open Share and press ✕ next to their email. They lose access right away.\nUseful actions: invite\n\n## Only the owner can invite\nInviting and removing people is limited to the workspace owner (👑 in the Share list). Everyone else can still edit everything inside it.\nUseful actions: invite\n\n## I can't sign in\n• Use a normal browser window (Chrome, Edge, Safari). Some in-app browsers block the Google pop-up.\n• If a pop-up blocker appears, allow pop-ups for this site and try again.\n• Make sure you're on lumenspaceapp.github.io.\n• Invited by email? Open the link from that email and confirm the same address.\nUseful actions: signin, check\n\n## Sign out or switch account\nClick your name at the bottom of the sidebar → Sign out. Then sign in again with the other Google account.\n\n## Change my avatar or name\nOpen Settings → Your profile → Change avatar to pick from 14 avatars, your Google photo, or your initial. It shows on chat, tasks, comments and the team directory. Job title and department live in Company & HR → Edit my profile.\nUseful actions: avatar, settings\n\n## Search everything\nPress Ctrl K (or click Search in the sidebar) to find tasks, people, deals, leads, contacts, files and apps, and to run commands like “Toggle dark mode”.\nUseful actions: search\n\n## Keyboard shortcuts\nCtrl K search · Ctrl  sidebar · Ctrl Shift L dark mode · Ctrl / open Lumi · in chat, Enter sends and Shift Enter adds a new line.\n\n## Move or reorder things\nComputer: drag a task card between columns on the Kanban board (and deals between stages in CRM).\nPhone: press and hold a card until it lifts, then drag it.\nUseful actions: tasks\n\n## Where did pages go?\nLumen is set up as a team workspace right now: Tasks, Chat, Feed, Calendar, CRM, Company & HR, Drive and Automation. Notion-style pages are switched off, but nothing was deleted. Ask the site owner if you need them back. For notes, try a task description, a Feed post or a file in Drive.\nUseful actions: tasks, drive\n\n## Tasks and projects\nOpen Tasks and press + New task. Pick the responsible person, participants (co-assignees), observers, a deadline, tags and a project. Views: List, Kanban, Deadlines, Planner (drag a card to plan it), Calendar and Gantt (drag bars to change dates). In a task you can add subtasks, a checklist, files, comments with @mentions, and link related tasks.\nUseful actions: tasks\n\n## Recurring tasks, reminders and templates\nInside a task: Repeat creates the next copy when you finish it, Remind me pings you at a time you choose, and the Start timer tracks time against an estimate. Tick Check the result when it's done to approve work before it closes (you get Approve / Send back). Use ⋯ → Save as template, then From template next to New task. Deleted tasks go to the Recycle bin tab. Efficiency is the share of your tasks finished on time in the last 30 days.\nUseful actions: tasks\n\n## Chat and messages\nIn Chat & Calls: message a teammate from the People list, or press New chat for a private group with chosen members. Channels are open to everyone; broadcast channels only let admins post. Hover a message to reply, forward, pin, react, edit or delete it. Attach files, paste images, or drop files into the chat. You'll see Seen and typing…, and the search box finds messages in all your chats.\nUseful actions: chat\n\n## Video calls\nPress 📹 Video call in a chat (or on Home). It opens a free Jitsi Meet room in a new tab and posts a “Join call” button so others can jump in.\nUseful actions: chat\n\n## Feed, announcements and polls\nIn Feed, write a Post, Announcement, Poll, Appreciation, Event (adds it to the calendar and invites people) or File post. Use To: to pick everyone, certain people or departments. Announcements have an I've read it button and show who has read them. @mention people in posts and comments; like, reply and attach files. Filters find posts by text, author, date and type.\nUseful actions: feed\n\n## Calendar and events\nIn Calendar press + Event, or click a time slot. Add attendees and they get an invitation to Accept / Maybe / Decline (pending ones are under Invitations). Events can repeat, remind you, book a meeting room (manage them under Rooms), include a video call link and files. My calendar events are private to you and your attendees. Views: month, week, day and agenda; drag your events to move or resize them.\nUseful actions: calendar\n\n## CRM: leads, deals and pipelines\nIn CRM, add leads and deals and drag deals between stages (Kanban), or switch to List, Activities or Calendar. Use the pipeline switcher → Configure pipelines to add pipelines and edit stages. Convert a lead into a contact and deal from its panel. Analytics shows the funnel, won vs lost, revenue and a leaderboard.\nUseful actions: crm\n\n## CRM activities, history and recycle bin\nOpen any deal, lead, contact or company and plan a call, meeting, task or email with a deadline; My activities lists everything you have to do. The timeline shows comments and every change (history). Deleted records go to the Recycle bin (⋯ menu). Find duplicates in ⋯ merges records with the same email, phone or name.\nUseful actions: crm\n\n## Import, export and custom fields\nIn each CRM list, the ⋯ menu has Import CSV (match your columns, preview, then import) and Export CSV. Configure fields adds your own fields to deals, leads, contacts or companies. Smart processes (header ⋯) let you track your own kind of item with its own stages.\nUseful actions: crm\n\n## Products, estimates and invoices\nIn CRM → Products build your catalog. Open a deal to add products, then Create estimate or Create invoice (or use the Estimates / Invoices tabs). Numbers are automatic; set your logo, address and bank details under Company details. Print / Save as PDF makes a ready-to-send document; mark invoices paid, and convert an accepted estimate into an invoice.\nUseful actions: crm\n\n## Web forms that create leads\nIn CRM → Forms press + New form, choose the fields and who gets the leads, and publish. Share the link, a QR code or the embed code for your website. Every answer becomes a lead automatically and the responsible person is notified. Forms need a shared workspace.\nUseful actions: crm\n\n## Change the currency\nOpen the CRM and use the currency menu (INR, USD, EUR, GBP, AED) next to + New deal. All deal amounts and totals switch right away.\nUseful actions: crm\n\n## Booking clients\nIn Booking, add Resources (people, rooms, equipment) and Services (length and price), then click a free slot in the schedule to book a client. Drag bookings to move them; mark them confirmed, late, done or no-show and paid. Clients shows visit history, and Settings sets opening hours. Linked people get a reminder 15 minutes before.\n\n## Inventory and stock\nIn Inventory, add a warehouse and products, then create a Receipt when goods arrive and press Conduct to add stock. Sales orders, Transfers and Write-offs reduce or move stock the same way. The Stock tab shows quantities per warehouse and warns about low stock; Analytics shows value and movements.\n\n## Request time off (leave)\nIn Company & HR press 🌴 Request time off, pick the type and dates and send. Your manager (the head of your department) approves or declines it under Requests, and you get notified. Requests also shows your remaining days per type; approved time off appears on the absence chart and Home.\n\n## Org chart, reports, shifts and meetings\nStructure is the org chart: admins add departments, heads and people. Reports: write your weekly report and your manager scores it. Schedules: plan shifts per person and day. Meetings: agenda, live minutes and decisions that become tasks. Worktime shows hours, late arrivals and a monthly report.\n\n## Workgroups and Scrum\nIn Workgroups press + Create: each group gets its own feed, tasks, calendar, files, chat and members, and can be open, closed (join on request) or secret. Choose type Scrum for a backlog, sprints with story points, epics, a burndown chart and velocity.\n\n## Admins, guests and permissions\nThe workspace owner and admins open Access & roles from the workspace menu (or Settings → Manage access). Set each person as admin, member or guest, and choose which apps each role can view or edit. Apps someone can't open are hidden for them.\n\n## Time off and team directory\nCompany & HR has the employee directory, an org chart by department, and the Absence chart. Press + Time off to add vacation, sick leave, remote or a trip. Absences show on Home and the Calendar.\nUseful actions: company\n\n## Clock in / track my hours\nPress ▶ Start day on Home (or Company & HR → Time tracking). Pause for breaks and End when done. A timer appears in the top bar, and the weekly report shows everyone's hours.\nUseful actions: company\n\n## Drive: shared files\nDrop files onto Drive or press Upload. Create folders, preview images and PDFs, and add links for big files (free plan: about 700 KB per uploaded file).\nUseful actions: drive\n\n## Automation rules\nIn Automation → Rules press + New rule (or pick a quick start): choose When something happens (deal stage, new lead, task done, booking, invoice paid, time off requested…), optional Only if conditions (e.g. amount over 50,000), and Then what Lumen does (notify, create a task, assign, move the deal, post to chat, start an approval). Each rule has an on/off switch and a run log.\nUseful actions: automation\n\n## Approvals, requests and expense reports\nPress 📝 Start a process in Automation, pick a request type (Purchase request, Expense report, General approval or your own), fill it in and send. It goes to your manager (and admins if the template says so); you're notified at each step. Approvers find it under Approvals → Waiting for me. Admins edit templates under Approvals → Templates.\nUseful actions: automation\n\n## Process boards and lists\nAutomation → RPA gives you boards where items move through stages with responsible people per stage (try the Hiring example). Automation → Lists are simple databases (equipment register, supplier list…) with your own columns, filters and CSV import/export.\nUseful actions: automation\n\n## Notifications\nNew chat messages, task assignments, mentions, comments and announcements pop up as a card with a soft chime, and the 🔔 bell (top right) keeps the list; “Mark all read” clears it. To get them while Lumen is in the background, click **Turn on** in the bell menu (or **Settings → Notifications**) and allow notifications. There you can also mute the sound, choose **All messages** or **DMs & @mentions** for chat, and **Send a test**. If it says Blocked, click the 🔒 icon next to the address and allow Notifications. Events remind you 10 minutes before, and you get a daily nudge for tasks due today.\nUseful actions: settings\n\n## Dark mode, colours and glass\nOpen Settings: Appearance (light / dark / system), accent colour, Glass blur and Glass transparency (changes show live behind the window), and animations on/off. Ctrl Shift L toggles dark mode.\nUseful actions: settings, theme\n\n## It feels slow\nGlass effects and animations use the graphics card. In Settings, turn Animations off and lower Glass blur. Closing other heavy tabs helps too.\nUseful actions: settings\n\n## Use Lumen on my phone\nOpen lumenspaceapp.github.io on your phone. To install it: Chrome → ⋮ → Add to Home screen; iPhone Safari → Share → Add to Home Screen. On a phone the sidebar opens with ☰, and you long-press to drag.\n\n## Changes or fixes aren't showing\nDo a hard refresh: Ctrl Shift R (Mac: Cmd Shift R). On a phone, close the tab and open it again. Lumen checks for the newest version every time it loads.\nUseful actions: reload\n\n## Offline and syncing\nEverything saves automatically: the top bar says Saved (private) or Synced (shared). Shared workspaces keep working offline and sync when you're back online. If it says “Sync failed”, check your connection, then run Check my setup.\nUseful actions: check\n\n## The old address\nLumen moved to lumenspaceapp.github.io. The old address forwards here. If you had private pages there, open the old address once and press Move my pages & continue.\n\n## Delete a shared workspace\nOwner only: open Share → Delete shared workspace. It permanently deletes all its pages and data for every member.\nUseful actions: invite";
